74 sacks are harvested per day, and 71 sacks are discarded per day. To find the number of sacks they will have after 51 days, subtract the number of discarded sacks from the number of harvested sacks: 74 sacks (harvested) - 71 sacks (discarded) = 3 sacks (net harvest per day) Then, multiply the net harvest per day by the number of days: 3 sacks per day × 51 days = 153 sacks Therefore, they will have 153 sacks of oranges after 51 days of harvest.

